tement export-connected then accept'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols bgp export export-connected', 'parent_command': ['family inet unicast'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `redistribute connected` command:\\n\\n##\\nset policy-options policy-statement export-connected term 1 from protocol direct\\nset policy-options policy-statement export-connected then accept\\nset protocols bgp export export-connected\\n##\\n\\nThis Juniper configuration:\\n1. Creates a policy statement called \"export-connected\"\\n2. Matches directly connected routes (equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"connected\") \\n3. Accepts/redistributes those routes\\n4. Applies the policy as a BGP export policy\\n\\nThe end result is the same as Cisco\\'s `redistribute connected` - it advertises directly connected networks via BGP.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols bgp export export-connected'}]]": 1,
